        "Nationally, the Association of Indian Universities issues equivalence certificates for international qualifications, including the IB Diploma, and many universities request one. CUET-UG serves as the gateway for central universities and is open to students from any board. JEE Main and JEE Advanced, and NEET-UG, publish their own subject and marks criteria in their information bulletins, which should be read directly and never assumed from a forum.",
        "Abroad, predicted grades open the conversation. British universities make conditional offers in IB points with subject minimums, American colleges weigh essays and activities alongside grades, and other countries publish their own conversion tables. A strong, consistent record in Maths and the sciences travels best.",
