  faqs: [
    { question: "Is there an IB or IGCSE school in Vaijapur?", answer: "Not one that we could confirm, either in Vaijapur or in Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar. The town's schools run the Maharashtra State Board, CBSE or ICSE syllabuses. Confirmed IB campuses sit in Pune and Mumbai, which is why families here generally keep the current school and layer an online tutor on top instead of relocating a child." },
    { question: "Will an IB Gram tutor visit my home in Vaijapur?", answer: "No. Our tutors do not visit homes in Vaijapur; home visits are offered only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. A Vaijapur lesson is live teaching on screen: the student sits at home with a laptop, the tutor appears on video and writes on a shared whiteboard, so the experience is private tuition in everything but physical presence." },
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor for my child in Vaijapur?", answer: "Write to us with the programme, subject and level, your child's current standing and the exam session they are aiming at. We then look across India for tutors who have recently taught that exact course, since Vaijapur has no local pool of IB teachers, and propose one with a short reason. A free trial lesson follows; if it does not suit, we offer someone else." },
    { question: "Can my child sit IGCSE exams from Vaijapur without changing school?", answer: "In most cases yes, as a private candidate attached to an exam centre. The sequence is to choose a board, settle the syllabus code and tier, then ask a centre, often in Pune, Mumbai or Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar, whether it takes private entries and by what date. Lessons run online and leave the school timetable alone. Start the centre enquiry early, as dates and places vary." },
    { question: "What does IB or IGCSE tuition cost for a Vaijapur family?", answer: "We do not publish a rate card. The figure you receive depends on the programme and level, how long and how often sessions run, and how much recent experience the tutor has with your specification, and it comes in writing before you book anything. Where you live makes no difference because nobody travels. The first lesson is free, so nothing is paid until you have seen the teaching." },
    { question: "What happens in the free trial lesson?", answer: "The proposed tutor and your child work on an actual topic from the syllabus on video, with no fee and no obligation. Expect questions that show where understanding is solid or shaky, and a clear explanation of one or two ideas. After the session you get a plan for the first month and the rate in writing, and you decide whether to go ahead, ask for changes or see another tutor." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with my IB Internal Assessment or Extended Essay?", answer: "Tutors can coach the process, not produce the work. That means unpacking the criteria, helping a student narrow a question to something answerable, talking through how to gather data, and giving candid comments on drafts the student has written. Anything written, rewritten or supplied by a tutor for assessment would breach IB academic integrity rules and could cost the qualification, so we never do it." },
    { question: "My child studies in a Marathi-medium or semi-English school. Can IB or IGCSE tuition still work?", answer: "It can, with deliberate attention to written English. Students from semi-English schools usually know technical terms well but have written few long explanations. Tutors teach what each command word requires, set a short written answer every week and mark it against the real scheme, so that clarity of expression and subject knowledge grow together instead of one lagging behind." },
    { question: "Which IB subjects can be matched for a student in Vaijapur?", answer: "Nearly every Diploma subject is possible: the two Maths courses, the three sciences, Economics, Business Management, Computer Science, Psychology, Geography, English A and Hindi B, plus TOK. Marathi A: Literature is checked when we read your brief. Send the subject, HL or SL and the exam session, and we will tell you straight away whether a suitable specialist is free." },
    { question: "Do you teach younger students in IB PYP and MYP?", answer: "We do. For PYP the work is reading, writing, number sense and the research habits behind the Exhibition, in short, regular sessions. For MYP it is criterion-based assignments in Sciences, Maths and Language and Literature, plus support for the Personal Project journal. Without an IB school in Vaijapur, these lessons often carry routines that a transferred child would otherwise drop." },
    { question: "What if power or internet fails during an online lesson in Vaijapur?", answer: "Message the tutor as soon as you can and rejoin when the connection is back; a mobile hotspot is a useful backup. A lost half hour can normally be recovered by moving another session that week. Summer power cuts and heavy monsoon days are the likeliest culprits, so keep drafts and mock papers a few days ahead of any deadline." },
    { question: "When should a Vaijapur student begin IB Diploma or IGCSE tuition?", answer: "Ideally when the course begins, which means Class 11 for the Diploma and Grade 9 for IGCSE. The early months are when written-English habits, command words and the first Internal Assessment plan are easiest to settle. A later start still works; the tutor then concentrates on the highest-value topics and on timed papers ahead of the next exam series." },
    { question: "Can my child prepare for MHT-CET, JEE or NEET alongside IB or IGCSE?", answer: "Many do, and it is manageable with an honest timetable. Content overlaps across Maths, Physics, Chemistry and Biology, yet entrance papers and IB or IGCSE papers are written in different styles, so each needs its own practice. Our tutors cover the IB or IGCSE side; entrance coaching is a separate job. Read each exam's current eligibility rules for your board before committing." },
    { question: "Is Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel more practical for a private candidate near Vaijapur?", answer: "Whichever has a centre, dates and subject list that work for you; neither is easier in itself. Cambridge holds its main series in May-June and October-November, Edexcel in January and May-June. Ask centres in Pune, Mumbai or Chhatrapati Sambhajinagar what they accept, choose one board, and keep all past papers and mark schemes from it." },
    { question: "Will Indian universities accept IB or IGCSE results from a Vaijapur student?", answer: "Generally yes, after the right paperwork. The Association of Indian Universities issues equivalence for the IB Diploma and IGCSE-based qualifications, central universities largely admit through CUET-UG, and MHT-CET, JEE and NEET each set their own conditions for other-board candidates. Apply for equivalence early in Class 12 and check every institution's rules directly." },
    { question: "Can lessons pause for Diwali, Ganeshotsav and Eid?", answer: "They can. Most families keep one weekday evening and one weekend slot, and agree with the tutor which festival days to skip or shift. Since the lessons are online, an extra session before a mock or exam series slots in easily, and no one has to travel to catch up." },
    { question: "What if the tutor is not the right fit?", answer: "Say so and we will find someone else. We check progress every few weeks, and a change of tutor is routine, not a favour. The free first lesson exists to expose a poor match early, and because rates are fixed in writing at the start, switching does not bring surprises." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram affiliated with any school or board named on this page?", answer: "No. We are an independent tutoring service. Nothing links us to the IB, Cambridge, Pearson or any school, college or university mentioned here, and we do not speak for them. The names are on this page so you can see the real options. Decisions about admission, exam entry and equivalence rest with those bodies." },
  ],

